\subsection{A benchmark-protected validation protocol}\label{sec:v13-rp}
The protocol combines a six-point penalty menu, longer validation and a corrected-rank historical default. It selects the lowest validation loss over 156 weekly observations or 5,760 FX records, switching only when paired improvement strictly exceeds one HAC standard error. Across 60 weekly comparisons, median excess falls from 14.63\% to 0.00\%, but 8 still lose by more than ten percent, missing the prewritten protection criterion. Both FX periods retain their ordinary-regression gains; the worst weekly excess remains 80.98\% (Figure~\ref{fig:v13-rp}). The rule was designed after earlier findings and uses inspected evaluation periods, so this check is retrospective.

\begin{figure}[htbp]\centering
\includegraphics[width=.98\linewidth]{figures/v13-rp.pdf}
\caption{Ordinary regression and the benchmark-default protocol relative to matched historical headroom. Every planned comparison is complete: 34 CFTC, 26 New York Fed and two FX cases; points retain each outcome, including large losses. Separate vertical scales preserve each source's distribution without pooling native exposure units.}\label{fig:v13-rp}
\end{figure}

